cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, code, or methodology in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Artifact-Resilient Cardiorespiratory Triage using PPG and Conformal Prediction"
authors:
  - family-names: "BDA Project Contributors"
    given-names: ""
abstract: >-
  An end-to-end Python pipeline for continuous respiratory rate estimation
  from photoplethysmography (PPG) biosignals using XGBoost and split conformal
  prediction. Evaluated under strict patient-disjoint 5-fold cross-validation on
  the 53-patient PhysioNet BIDMC ICU cohort, targeting CPU-only hardware
  execution with adaptive uncertainty quantification and safe clinical abstention.
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-17"
license: MIT
